  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 7, 'Digital health supply chain architecture framework'. Top row: SHARED SERVICES, whose foundational components are facility, product (highlighted) and supplier registries; DATA SERVICES, with analytics (supply chain reports, data warehouse) and traceability (track and trace, product verification); and Digital Ecosystems (quality, health management information, regulatory, and finance and insurance systems). A middle INTEROPERABILITY LAYER of enabling components: authentication, encryption, transformation, orchestration, validation and translation. Bottom: HEALTH SUPPLY CHAIN INFORMATION SYSTEMS — forecasting and planning, order management, warehouse management, cold chain management, procurement, supplier and contract management, transportation management and dispensing — beside External systems (global platforms, manufacturer systems, data repositories).",
